{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 123, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With node 2 disconnected from the output, a direct conv path from input to output adds much-needed capacity and signal."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual shortcut where none existed helps, whereas replacing a 3x3 conv with skip loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 4 when edge 5 is already none leaves only edge 3 into the output, severely starving the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-output edge when node 2 does not feed the output cuts most or all paths to the output node."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 5 activates node 2's contribution, a larger gain than swapping an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 none, node 1 is zero and edges 2 and 4 are wasted, so adding a conv there revives them."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learned 3x3 conv with parameter-free pooling loses representational capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv into node 2 only matters if node 2 reaches the output through edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 none, node 1 carries no signal, so a conv from node 1 to the output contributes